WEBVTT

00:13.854 --> 00:17.357
In my experience, once you talk to
people, they usually open up pretty

00:17.441 --> 00:18.275
quickly.

00:18.358 --> 00:21.278
People are always telling me that I seem
intimidating.

00:24.990 --> 00:27.617
I'm not very good at approaching
people on my own.

00:27.701 --> 00:30.203
Nice to find someone who shares
my love of manga!

00:33.498 --> 00:36.918
I had always been kinda bored
here since I hadn't found others I had

00:37.002 --> 00:38.003
much in common with.

00:41.298 --> 00:42.174
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:42.257 --> 00:43.091
Thank you.

00:43.175 --> 00:44.009
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:44.092 --> 00:44.926
Thank you.

00:45.010 --> 00:46.136
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

00:46.219 --> 00:47.429
- Thank you.
- No problem.

00:49.473 --> 00:53.351
What if the only reason someone felt
alone was because no one had found…

00:54.561 --> 00:55.604
The right key?

00:57.564 --> 00:59.649
- HAMBURGER BOM BOM
- And then that guy was like…

00:59.733 --> 01:01.818
Hey, Amamiya, are you even listening?

01:02.694 --> 01:04.446
Hm? Yeah, course I am!

01:05.489 --> 01:06.531
No, I'm not.

02:32.409 --> 02:34.744
THE RAMPARTS OF ICE

02:38.582 --> 02:40.584
EPISODE 2 LOCKSMITH

02:43.503 --> 02:45.213
Now come on, let's go have some fun.

02:45.297 --> 02:46.673
I'm not going anywhere!

02:46.756 --> 02:48.675
Oh, what should I do?

02:50.177 --> 02:51.011
And frustrated.

02:52.387 --> 02:53.722
- And pissed off.
- Come on.

02:54.389 --> 02:56.057
- It'll be super fun!
- I told you…

02:56.683 --> 02:57.851
I'm not going anywhere!

02:58.977 --> 03:00.437
Leave me alone.

03:00.520 --> 03:01.688
Seriously.

03:04.816 --> 03:05.650
Bye.

03:08.486 --> 03:09.863
Sorry. Are you okay?

03:10.572 --> 03:12.824
Oh! I knew it! It was you.

03:14.492 --> 03:15.702
Mr. Giraffe.

03:17.370 --> 03:19.539
Sorry I ignored you, but I couldn't see
you.

03:19.623 --> 03:20.457
Oh, um, well…

03:21.833 --> 03:23.835
- Hm?
- Please pretend to be my friend.

03:24.544 --> 03:25.378
I'm sorry.

03:25.462 --> 03:28.715
Please just stay with me until these
two guys leave me alone.

03:29.466 --> 03:30.300
Huh?

03:30.842 --> 03:32.969
SWIFT

03:33.053 --> 03:35.764
Okay, well, I found my friend, so
I'm fine now. Bye.

03:35.847 --> 03:37.057
Huh? What? What? Huh?

03:37.140 --> 03:39.392
BLURRY

03:40.310 --> 03:41.686
Does she know these guys?

03:42.229 --> 03:44.064
- Stare…
- I guess not.

03:45.982 --> 03:48.151
HURRY

03:48.235 --> 03:50.153
High schoolers these days are such
freaks.

03:50.237 --> 03:51.071
Right?

03:52.739 --> 03:54.032
Thank you very much.

03:55.242 --> 03:57.494
Huh? But I didn't do anything, did I?

03:58.245 --> 04:00.038
Wait, didn't you know them?

04:01.623 --> 04:03.500
They came up and started talking to me.

04:03.583 --> 04:05.252
Wow, you're so popular!

04:06.836 --> 04:07.796
It's not like that!

04:08.713 --> 04:12.300
Uh. Or at least, um, I mean, back there…

04:12.801 --> 04:14.594
This wasn't like that.

04:15.762 --> 04:19.766
They were the kind of guys who only cared
about their own enjoyment, not mine.

04:21.017 --> 04:22.560
They talked down to me.

04:23.395 --> 04:25.397
I-I'm not interested in guys like that.

04:26.523 --> 04:27.357
Or…

04:29.025 --> 04:29.859
Oh.

04:29.943 --> 04:32.070
Agh, why am I blabbering at him
like this?

04:33.029 --> 04:34.948
Oh man, I'm totally oversharing.

04:36.533 --> 04:37.742
I'm gonna weird him out.

04:38.368 --> 04:39.202
Hmm.

04:40.120 --> 04:43.164
So wait, are you saying I should've
knocked their lights out?

04:43.248 --> 04:44.082
What?

04:44.165 --> 04:46.126
Oh, n-n-no, you don't have to go
that far.

04:46.209 --> 04:47.085
Are you sure?

04:48.295 --> 04:49.129
And I'm sorry.

04:49.212 --> 04:52.382
I feel bad.
I kind of used you to get away from them.

04:52.882 --> 04:55.302
Huh? What? Why? It's totally fine.

04:55.969 --> 04:58.096
That's not the kind of thing that
would upset me.

04:58.179 --> 04:59.014
You're good.

05:01.391 --> 05:03.059
Do you live around here, Himuro?

05:03.643 --> 05:05.770
No, I was heading to the community
center.

05:05.854 --> 05:07.689
Huh? Hey, that's where I'm going!

05:08.398 --> 05:10.108
Do you wanna walk there together?

05:13.236 --> 05:14.070
Mm-hm.

05:20.452 --> 05:23.330
Since there are no club activities
during the exam preparation period, your

05:23.413 --> 05:24.831
daily routine tends to get disrupted.

05:24.914 --> 05:26.666
Oh, homeroom is going way over!

05:26.750 --> 05:28.251
Koyun, I'm so sorry to keep you waiting!

05:28.335 --> 05:29.544
Set up a study schedule.

05:31.296 --> 05:32.172
So… uh…

05:33.423 --> 05:34.257
Hm?

05:37.052 --> 05:39.387
Can you, uh, tell me your name, please?

05:40.388 --> 05:42.766
Oh, right. I guess I never actually
introduced myself, did I?

05:42.849 --> 05:43.725
Sorry about that.

05:45.060 --> 05:47.103
Yota. Just call me Yota.

05:48.188 --> 05:50.231
I can't just call him by his first name!

05:51.066 --> 05:52.359
Nice to meet you, Himuro.

05:53.026 --> 05:54.903
Oh. Well, um…

05:55.487 --> 05:58.615
My name… isn't Himuro, it's Hikawa.

05:58.698 --> 06:00.033
What? I'm so sorry!

06:00.533 --> 06:02.369
I wish you would've told me sooner.

06:07.040 --> 06:09.501
So… how far are we from the community
center?

06:10.001 --> 06:11.711
I'm directionally challenged.

06:12.253 --> 06:14.255
About five more minutes and we're there.

06:15.090 --> 06:15.924
Five minutes.

06:17.133 --> 06:19.135
Can we keep this conversation going?

06:24.682 --> 06:27.310
So, Hikawa… Are you and Miki close?

06:28.269 --> 06:29.687
Oh. Well, um…

06:30.397 --> 06:31.272
We're old friends.

06:31.356 --> 06:33.858
We went to the same elementary and
middle schools.

06:34.484 --> 06:35.693
Huh. That's really cool.

06:40.448 --> 06:41.616
Uh.

06:42.492 --> 06:43.618
Since junior high…

06:44.160 --> 06:47.163
So does that mean he's seen what she's
really like, then?

06:47.247 --> 06:48.581
Modern Miki!

06:49.124 --> 06:53.294
You know, to be honest, I thought Miki
was way better the way she used to be!

06:53.795 --> 06:54.879
I think so too.

06:55.380 --> 06:56.256
Oh, good.

06:56.339 --> 06:58.967
It bugs me.
I wanna shout it from the rooftops.

06:59.050 --> 07:01.219
It just feels like such a waste, y'know?

07:01.302 --> 07:02.303
Mm.

07:09.686 --> 07:11.271
- [Cracking up} Hold up.
- HAMBURGER BOM BOM

07:11.354 --> 07:12.605
Seriously?

07:13.773 --> 07:15.066
Wait, is that Yota?

07:15.150 --> 07:16.067
Hm?

07:16.734 --> 07:17.777
Oh yeah, you're right.

07:17.861 --> 07:20.029
No way… The girl next to him is…

07:22.073 --> 07:22.907
Huh?

07:23.700 --> 07:25.660
MEITEN COMMUNITY CENTER

07:25.743 --> 07:26.661
Uh.

07:28.079 --> 07:28.997
- Shh.
- Shh.

07:29.956 --> 07:31.374
Here, we saved you a seat.

07:31.458 --> 07:32.292
Oh. Thanks.

07:32.792 --> 07:33.960
But I don't understand.

07:34.043 --> 07:35.920
What're you both doing here together?

07:37.046 --> 07:39.132
- Together?
- Good question.

07:42.552 --> 07:43.386
Well?

07:44.053 --> 07:45.472
Still waiting for an answer.

07:45.555 --> 07:46.473
Quiet.

07:46.556 --> 07:48.766
Uh. What're you…

07:49.851 --> 07:51.352
Oh! I'm so sorry.

07:53.897 --> 07:54.898
This came out of nowhere!

07:54.981 --> 07:58.943
You guys should've warned me beforehand
instead of just springing it on me like

07:59.027 --> 08:01.112
- that!
- I actually told her not to text you.

08:01.196 --> 08:02.614
So then it'd be a surprise.

08:02.697 --> 08:03.573
Really, Koyun?

08:03.656 --> 08:05.783
Can't believe you played along with him!

08:06.826 --> 08:08.995
Anyway, did you punch the guys who
were messing with her?

08:09.078 --> 08:11.789
- Did you knock their lights out?
- No.

08:11.873 --> 08:13.333
Hikawa said I didn't have to.

08:13.875 --> 08:15.710
I told him it really wasn't necessary.

08:15.793 --> 08:16.794
Lame!

08:18.338 --> 08:19.964
Are you two taking the same train?

08:20.048 --> 08:21.382
I'll walk you to the station.

08:21.466 --> 08:22.425
Aw, thank you!

08:24.260 --> 08:26.471
Yota, do you always go to that
study room?

08:26.554 --> 08:28.097
Uh, yeah, actually.

08:28.848 --> 08:32.268
My younger brother and sister are
still little, so it can get pretty

08:32.352 --> 08:33.186
noisy at home.

08:33.269 --> 08:35.188
Mmm-hmm! What age?

08:35.688 --> 08:38.274
Oh, my brother and sister are both
three years old.

08:38.358 --> 08:41.319
- They're fraternal twins.
- Wow, that's quite an age gap.

08:42.028 --> 08:45.865
So, part of it's to get away from the
noise at home, but, in general, I just

08:45.949 --> 08:48.451
- concentrate way better at the center.
- Oh, I get that.

08:48.535 --> 08:50.745
I didn't scroll on my phone even one
time.

08:50.828 --> 08:52.121
I'm very proud of myself.

08:52.622 --> 08:53.998
That's not that hard.

08:55.667 --> 08:57.126
- Oh.
- Huh?

08:57.210 --> 08:58.044
Hold on a sec.

08:58.795 --> 09:00.171
All that studying…

09:00.255 --> 09:02.674
Gotta replenish my energy with
some sugar.

09:02.757 --> 09:04.634
Ooh, good idea!

09:05.927 --> 09:07.178
I think I'll get one too.

09:12.183 --> 09:14.102
He's taller than the vending machine.

09:14.185 --> 09:15.186
Must be nice.

09:16.980 --> 09:18.648
I wish I had been born that tall.

09:19.857 --> 09:21.234
Go ahead, pick what you want.

09:21.317 --> 09:22.235
Oh, are you sure?

09:22.860 --> 09:24.362
Sweet red bean soup, right?

09:25.071 --> 09:26.364
You know me so well!

09:26.447 --> 09:27.740
This was nice of you, Yota.

09:27.824 --> 09:30.159
I'll make sure to get yours the
next time.

09:30.660 --> 09:31.619
Whoa! Ah, what happened?!

09:31.703 --> 09:33.329
Whoa! Oh! Ay, ay, ay, ay, ay…

09:33.413 --> 09:34.747
FLUSTER

09:34.831 --> 09:37.750
Why'd you have a zillion coins instead of
just using bills?!

09:37.834 --> 09:39.377
- I know, sorry.
- Oh, jeez.

09:39.460 --> 09:42.589
NATURAL SPARKLING LEMON WATER
REFRESHING AND DELICIOUS APPLE JUICE

09:42.672 --> 09:43.673
- Want a drink?
- Huh?

09:43.756 --> 09:45.216
- What about you, Hikawa?
- Me?

09:45.300 --> 09:46.175
Oh, no, uh, I- I…

09:46.259 --> 09:47.093
- Hm.
- Hm.

09:47.677 --> 09:49.846
Well, Miki will just have to pick
for you.

09:49.929 --> 09:51.139
You got it.

09:52.015 --> 09:54.434
COCOA, SWEET RED BEAN SOUP,
AMAZAKE CORN POTAGE

09:54.517 --> 09:56.936
But I want the sweet red bean soup,
so she'll get the sweet red

09:57.020 --> 09:57.854
Hmm, I think she wants the corn
potage soup.

09:57.937 --> 09:59.272
But I want the sweet red bean soup,
so she'll get the sweet red

09:59.355 --> 10:00.189
Seriously?

10:00.273 --> 10:03.484
Well, I want us to drink the
same thing so we can talk about how

10:03.568 --> 10:04.652
delicious it is!

10:05.778 --> 10:06.821
So self-centered.

10:08.031 --> 10:09.073
They seem so close.

10:13.244 --> 10:16.914
I know I mentioned this earlier, but
we went to the same cram school back

10:16.998 --> 10:17.832
in junior high.

10:17.915 --> 10:20.877
So me, Miki, and Minato used to hang out
all the time.

10:20.960 --> 10:24.547
Yup. After cram school, we'd always get
something to eat and just talk.

10:24.631 --> 10:27.383
Mina-
Oh, wait, you're talking about Amamiya?

10:27.467 --> 10:29.636
Whoa! Koyun, I had no idea you knew him!

10:30.678 --> 10:32.555
Well, I wouldn't say I know him.

10:33.181 --> 10:34.766
STRETCH

10:35.642 --> 10:37.644
Oh no, was he bullying you again?

10:37.727 --> 10:38.853
Again?

10:39.646 --> 10:40.521
Uh, well, no, he…

10:41.439 --> 10:42.690
I'm sorry about him.

10:43.399 --> 10:44.984
I swear, you can just ignore him.

10:45.068 --> 10:46.069
What?

10:46.152 --> 10:48.780
Have you and Amamiya had a falling out
or something?

10:49.656 --> 10:50.990
No, I'm just kidding.

10:53.201 --> 10:55.370
Koyun, Yota, and Minato…

10:56.204 --> 10:59.415
So, tell me, Hikawa, does everybody
around you call you Koyun?

11:01.459 --> 11:03.002
- Mm?
- Koyun!

11:03.086 --> 11:05.588
- Uh, yes?
- It's a pretty good nickname!

11:06.297 --> 11:08.591
- Yeah, right?
- Don't let it get to your head.

11:09.759 --> 11:12.512
I know I said it before, but just call me
Yota.

11:12.595 --> 11:15.056
I don't like to make things super
complicated.

11:15.139 --> 11:15.973
Or too formal.

11:16.057 --> 11:17.475
- Uh…
- Oh, I feel you.

11:17.558 --> 11:20.603
I prefer Miki to some dumb little
nickname.

11:21.312 --> 11:22.730
Hmm, is that so?

11:24.190 --> 11:25.274
Thanks again, Yota!

11:26.317 --> 11:27.443
Hey! See you tomorrow?

11:28.569 --> 11:29.529
Yep, I'll be there.

11:30.029 --> 11:31.531
Okay, have a great night.

11:32.156 --> 11:32.990
Yeah, see ya!

11:35.326 --> 11:36.244
See ya tomorrow.

11:46.295 --> 11:47.130
Hmm

11:52.677 --> 11:53.553
Koyuki…

11:54.095 --> 11:54.971
Hikawa…

11:58.307 --> 12:00.143
Has she… always gone here?

12:00.643 --> 12:02.603
I think her last name's Hikawa.

12:02.687 --> 12:03.688
She's in class two.

12:04.272 --> 12:06.607
I heard she's a loner, and super
unfriendly.

12:13.239 --> 12:16.033
Class two was the quiet class, if I
remember correctly.

12:17.535 --> 12:20.997
Maybe she just hasn't found anyone
else that she vibes with yet.

12:22.582 --> 12:26.419
I'd always been curious about her
whenever I saw her.

12:27.670 --> 12:28.588
She's alone again.

12:32.258 --> 12:33.092
SQUISH

12:33.760 --> 12:35.178
Every time I see her…

12:36.512 --> 12:37.346
I feel…

12:38.389 --> 12:39.807
Sorry for- Hm?

12:40.433 --> 12:41.976
INCOMING CALL

12:44.312 --> 12:47.190
Hey, Minato. Sorry, but can we meet up?

12:47.857 --> 12:49.317
I wanna talk about something.

12:50.151 --> 12:51.736
Yeah. No problem.

13:08.586 --> 13:10.254
So, what do you wanna talk about?

13:14.258 --> 13:15.092
Aren't you cold?

13:22.058 --> 13:22.934
I wanna break up.

13:27.772 --> 13:29.232
What makes you say that?

13:32.151 --> 13:33.402
I can't trust you.

13:34.904 --> 13:38.241
I mean, look, you're a very nice
guy, I'll give you that, but…

13:39.075 --> 13:39.909
I don't think…

13:40.451 --> 13:43.788
I don't think you ever really liked me,
did you, Minato?

13:45.039 --> 13:47.083
Your heart was never really in it.

13:50.044 --> 13:52.630
Did I do something wrong to make you
feel that way?

13:54.048 --> 13:56.759
Stop responding to everything with a
question.

13:56.843 --> 13:57.844
You always do that.

13:58.344 --> 14:00.596
Just show me how you really feel
for once!

14:06.811 --> 14:08.229
Know what I think?

14:09.397 --> 14:11.691
You don't have a real sense of self.

14:14.902 --> 14:15.736
I'm home.

14:18.114 --> 14:19.949
Wait, what were you doing out this late?

14:20.032 --> 14:21.409
Is something the matter?

14:21.492 --> 14:22.869
Mm? Nah, don't worry.

14:23.828 --> 14:24.996
It's nothing important.

14:28.916 --> 14:29.750
Yay!

14:30.585 --> 14:32.879
I mean, shoot, oh no, that really sucks,
buddy!

14:32.962 --> 14:36.757
I just got dumped. Can you at least
pretend to feel bad for me or something?

14:36.841 --> 14:38.134
How many times is this now?

14:38.217 --> 14:40.678
Yeah, at this point it's actually kind of
funny.

14:40.761 --> 14:43.347
But I'm sure you'll find another
girlfriend soon.

14:43.431 --> 14:45.558
What? Did you get dumped again, Amamiya?

14:46.058 --> 14:47.101
That's right.

14:47.602 --> 14:51.230
I was in the middle of studying last
night, and she called and asked me to

14:51.314 --> 14:53.691
- come meet her. Then dumped me.
- Oof, brutal.

14:53.774 --> 14:56.986
I always get dumped, and I just
keep asking myself…

14:58.863 --> 15:00.364
- How come?
- Huh?

15:00.448 --> 15:01.282
Well, I, uh…

15:01.365 --> 15:03.200
HE DOES THIS IF I DON'T KEEP AN EYE ON HIM

15:03.284 --> 15:04.118
- Ugh.
- Fujita, don't let him charm you like

15:04.201 --> 15:05.077
that! You can't look this guy in the eye
for more than three seconds!

15:05.161 --> 15:07.079
BA-DUMP, BA-DUMP

15:08.831 --> 15:11.083
- I'll hold him off. Run while you still
- Morning, everyone!

15:11.167 --> 15:12.001
- Can!
- What the…

15:12.084 --> 15:14.337
Seriously, Minato?
What have you done this time?

15:14.420 --> 15:16.172
- Jeez.
- I didn't do anything.

15:16.255 --> 15:18.007
Why do you assume that every time?

15:19.216 --> 15:20.843
Oh. That's right.

15:23.804 --> 15:24.639
Hm…

15:28.100 --> 15:31.520
I'm telling you, the school store's
a treasure trove if you go early.

15:31.604 --> 15:33.522
- Hey, Yota.
- Hm?

15:33.606 --> 15:36.317
Did I happen to see you walking
Hikawa home yesterday?

15:37.109 --> 15:38.611
I know what he'll say…

15:38.694 --> 15:40.655
Huh? No way, you've got it all wrong.

15:40.738 --> 15:41.948
It's not like that.

15:42.990 --> 15:44.116
- Oh, you saw us.
- Huh?

15:44.200 --> 15:45.034
Hm?

15:46.202 --> 15:49.372
We just happened to run into each other,
so we walked together.

15:52.583 --> 15:54.835
Oh, okay. So that's all?

15:55.336 --> 15:57.296
Just saying, 'cause you kinda…

16:01.133 --> 16:02.635
SCHOOL NURSE'S OFFICE

16:02.718 --> 16:03.552
Oh.

16:04.220 --> 16:07.181
Hey, Hikawa!
Why are you in the nurse's office?

16:07.264 --> 16:09.141
- Are you sick or hurt of something?
- Um.

16:09.225 --> 16:10.267
No, I just, I, um…

16:11.352 --> 16:12.520
Huh? Hey, what is it?

16:13.729 --> 16:14.772
Oh, Yota, hi.

16:15.940 --> 16:16.899
First name basis?

16:17.692 --> 16:18.901
Hey there, Koyun!

16:20.069 --> 16:20.903
Him too?

16:21.612 --> 16:22.655
Not feeling that well?

16:22.738 --> 16:23.698
Are you okay?

16:24.198 --> 16:26.784
Oh, I'm fine.
I'm just here to get close to the heater.

16:26.867 --> 16:29.662
But why's that? Do you think it's
that cold out today?

16:29.745 --> 16:31.914
You seen the weather? It's freezing.

16:31.998 --> 16:33.165
Got your contacts in?

16:33.249 --> 16:34.583
Jeez, it's like I don't even exist.

16:34.667 --> 16:36.585
- Yeah! I can see perfectly.
- Oh, good.

16:36.669 --> 16:37.545
Hey, Miss Hikawa.

16:38.045 --> 16:38.963
Oh!

16:39.046 --> 16:41.132
You're letting all of the precious heat
out.

16:41.215 --> 16:43.342
So, if you're going, would you close the
door?

16:43.426 --> 16:44.260
Go on, shoo!

16:45.011 --> 16:46.554
She got pretty mad at you there.

16:46.637 --> 16:48.180
Noriko is always like that.

16:48.681 --> 16:50.641
Hikawa, you going to the fourth floor?

16:52.018 --> 16:53.310
We're going upstairs too.

16:53.978 --> 16:54.979
Well, I…

16:56.022 --> 16:58.315
Gotta go to the first floor to, um…
my locker.

16:58.399 --> 16:59.233
My locker.

17:00.026 --> 17:00.860
Gotcha.

17:00.943 --> 17:02.111
BRISKLY

17:02.194 --> 17:04.572
- Well then, I'll just, uh…
- See ya in a bit!

17:06.115 --> 17:06.949
In a bit?

17:16.208 --> 17:18.878
Did they really "just happen" to run into
each other?

17:20.796 --> 17:23.966
Woo! I studied my butt off today!

17:24.050 --> 17:26.093
Then again, I always do.

17:26.177 --> 17:29.805
But to be honest, there're things I
still don't get, and sometimes I

17:29.889 --> 17:32.933
wanna talk things out and ask questions
while we're studying.

17:33.017 --> 17:35.686
Then after school tomorrow, wanna just
study in the classroom?

17:35.770 --> 17:37.354
I can help explain stuff.

17:37.438 --> 17:38.814
You're cool with that?

17:38.898 --> 17:41.776
Please! Share all your wisdom and smarts
with me, Sensei!

17:41.859 --> 17:43.652
Well, I don't know about all that.

17:43.736 --> 17:44.820
BAM

17:44.904 --> 17:46.614
Sensei! Oh no!

17:46.697 --> 17:47.615
Owie.

17:47.698 --> 17:48.699
Uh…

17:48.783 --> 17:50.618
Jeez, that looks like it hurt. You
alright?

17:50.701 --> 17:53.079
Eh, I bump my head into things all
the time.

17:54.538 --> 17:56.874
- Oh.
- Oy, Yota's class…

17:58.334 --> 17:59.752
Seems like it'll be noisy.

18:00.711 --> 18:02.296
- Hm.
- Don't worry.

18:02.379 --> 18:03.214
Huh?

18:03.297 --> 18:05.549
When the bell rings, the noisy ones all
leave.

18:05.633 --> 18:07.176
Yeah, they all go home.

18:07.259 --> 18:08.094
He just read my mind.

18:08.177 --> 18:09.011
I KIND OF LIKE IT

18:09.095 --> 18:09.386
Noise isn't really Koyun's vibe.

18:09.470 --> 18:10.554
How embarrassing.

18:14.016 --> 18:15.601
SPACE FOR ONE PERSON

18:16.102 --> 18:17.228
Huh.

18:20.022 --> 18:21.190
Let's play for it.

18:21.857 --> 18:23.692
- Rock, paper, sci-
- Rock, paper, sci-

18:23.776 --> 18:24.610
- Oh!
- Oh!

18:24.693 --> 18:25.653
- Go ahead, Sir!
- Go ahead, Sir!

18:25.736 --> 18:26.570
No, please sit.

18:26.654 --> 18:28.614
- I insist.
- No, it's okay. Take it.

18:28.697 --> 18:31.534
- PR face.
- We're getting off at the next station.

18:31.617 --> 18:32.451
What?

18:33.744 --> 18:37.706
Please use the stairs in the middle of
the platform to transfer to other lines.

18:39.208 --> 18:42.461
- Oh no! Hurry! Oh no, oh no, oh no, oh no,
- The doors on platform three are closing.

18:42.545 --> 18:43.379
Oh no!

18:48.092 --> 18:50.219
HUFF, HUFF

18:50.302 --> 18:53.222
- You could've just let him have it.
- I dunno, it just came out.

18:53.305 --> 18:54.765
Why did you have to lie to the man?!

18:54.849 --> 18:55.683
I was embarrassed!

18:55.766 --> 18:56.642
FOGGY

18:57.143 --> 19:00.563
Speaking of embarrassing, my heavy
breathing's fogged up the window.

19:07.153 --> 19:08.988
Oh no, you're making me laugh too!

19:12.533 --> 19:16.495
After finals, I'm back to working after
school, which means we won't be able to

19:16.579 --> 19:17.413
THEY TEND TO TALK A LITTLE MORE WHEN

19:17.496 --> 19:18.330
walk home together. walk home together.

19:18.414 --> 19:19.957
THEY ARE ABOUT TO SAY GOODBYE

19:20.040 --> 19:22.376
- Huh?
- You've never been right?

19:22.459 --> 19:24.170
I'll throw in a free smile for ya!

19:26.172 --> 19:27.006
Hmm.

19:28.090 --> 19:30.676
- Stylish burger! Yay!
- Honestly, I'm a bit intimidated

19:30.759 --> 19:32.428
by the idea of going there alone.

19:32.511 --> 19:34.430
BECAUSE I'M ONLY A HIGH SCHOOL STUDENT

19:34.513 --> 19:36.056
Their burgers are crazy expensive.

19:36.140 --> 19:38.642
If I ask the manager, he might give you a
discount!

19:38.726 --> 19:40.269
Sure, I'll knock some Yen off for ya.

19:40.352 --> 19:41.395
SHOP MANAGER

19:41.896 --> 19:44.690
If you're scared to go alone, you can
just drag Yota along?

19:44.773 --> 19:45.774
Mm.

19:45.858 --> 19:47.985
Wait, no, Yota has his after school club.

19:48.068 --> 19:49.111
Hm.

19:51.989 --> 19:53.073
Well, see ya later!

19:53.157 --> 19:56.076
- ROOM 201 HIKAWA
- See you later.

20:13.928 --> 20:14.762
Oh.

20:15.346 --> 20:16.305
The laundry.

20:27.900 --> 20:31.445
- Hm?
- Was I… smiling just now?

20:33.781 --> 20:34.615
Wait.

20:35.574 --> 20:39.411
I feel a lingering happiness from today,
and I'm actually looking forward to

20:39.495 --> 20:40.621
tomorrow.

20:42.915 --> 20:44.166
It's easier to be alone.

20:44.667 --> 20:45.501
I'm having fun.

20:46.001 --> 20:47.211
I don't want to get attached.

20:47.294 --> 20:48.796
I wanna see them again.

20:48.879 --> 20:50.172
I want to be left alone.

20:50.256 --> 20:51.632
I'm excited for tomorrow.

20:54.093 --> 20:57.137
I feel all of these feelings… and all
so deeply.

20:57.972 --> 20:58.973
But they conflict.

21:01.100 --> 21:03.811
So then… what is it I really want?

21:06.146 --> 21:08.565
I have no idea what I'm feeling.

21:13.112 --> 21:14.530
GRADE 1 CLASS 6

21:14.613 --> 21:16.573
- Did you get the homework at all? I was
- Sneak peak.

21:16.657 --> 21:19.076
Completely lost. I literally had to ask
my sister to explain it to me.

21:19.159 --> 21:20.035
Glad you made it.

21:20.119 --> 21:22.371
- Ha, yeah I know. I was so embarrassed,
- Hi. Good morning.

21:22.454 --> 21:24.123
She'll never let me live it down.

21:24.957 --> 21:26.917
Miki just said she's running behind.

21:27.835 --> 21:29.628
Oh, she texted me about it too.

21:30.671 --> 21:33.048
Class five's homeroom tends to run long.

21:33.674 --> 21:36.343
Hey, why don't I just create a new group
chat for us?

21:36.427 --> 21:37.511
Oh. Smart.

21:38.262 --> 21:40.931
- Wow.
- Oh, Minato. What's up?

21:41.849 --> 21:42.683
So are you two…

21:43.809 --> 21:44.727
Like, an item?

21:44.810 --> 21:45.936
Huh? What? No!

21:46.020 --> 21:47.021
We're not! No!

21:47.688 --> 21:49.606
Miki's gonna be joining us here soon.

21:49.690 --> 21:50.607
Miki too?

21:51.108 --> 21:52.651
That's such a random group.

21:52.735 --> 21:53.819
CLATTER

21:53.902 --> 21:55.779
Huh? W- wait, Minato?!

21:56.322 --> 21:58.574
Do you not want me to be here or
something?

21:58.657 --> 22:00.451
No, it's not that at all.

22:01.368 --> 22:03.078
Miki's acting more like herself.

22:05.831 --> 22:07.833
So… are you all studying together?

22:07.916 --> 22:09.335
That's right, you got it!

22:09.418 --> 22:10.377
I see.

22:16.175 --> 22:17.009
Sounds fun.

22:17.718 --> 22:18.802
Let's get to it!

22:23.140 --> 22:23.974
Huh?
